NAME
       mv - move or rename files

SYNOPSIS
       mv [-fiv] source ... target

DESCRIPTION
       Renames SOURCE to TARGET, or moves several SOURCEs into a
       directory. Within one filesystem the move is a rename and costs
       nothing; across filesystems the file is copied and the original
       removed.

OPTIONS
       -f     never prompt
       -i     prompt before overwriting an existing target
       -v     print each file as it is moved

SEE ALSO
       cp(1), rm(1)
